# NET G cell — the STAGE-1 pair's SECOND dispatcher arm, and the ABLATION
# HANDLE for the stage-1-only mechanism. set arm.
#
# ⚠ THIS CELL IS NOT ITSELF STAGE-1-ONLY — its list sibling
# `stage1_list_strsrc_filt.gg` is. Read that one for the class; this one is
# wrong at stage 0 too, and it is here for the two reasons below.
#
# AXIS CELL: comp-kind = set `{...}`  ·  source = String (codepoints)  ·
# destination = `auto` (the EMPTY result channel)  ·  FILTERED.
#
# ⚠ IT STILL RUNS THROUGH AN INSTRUMENT NO ORDINARY GATE PROVIDES. Every
# other self-host gate in the tree runs the STAGE-0 driver (the one Rust gg
# built), and `self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point` compares emitted C *text*,
# not behaviour.
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED. A pristine-HEAD stage-1 binary prints `0/false/false`
# here where `2/true/true` is correct; under the round's fix stage 1 prints
# `2/true/true`. ⚠ Unlike its list sibling, THIS cell is wrong at stage 0
# too (the same `0/false/false` — the §4 silent drop), so it is NOT by
# itself evidence of a stage-1-only class. It is here so the stage-1 pair
# samples a SECOND dispatcher arm and is provably not one cell twice.
#
# ⚠ THIS CELL IS ALSO THE ABLATION HANDLE FOR THE STAGE-1-ONLY MECHANISM.
# That mechanism — the self-host lowerer double-freeing on `(*b).clone()`
# where `b` came from `case Some(b)` on an `Option[Box[T]]` — is pinned by
# `known_gaps/sh_option_box_deref_clone_double_free.gg` and filed in
# `TODO.md` (grep `stage-1-only`). `lower_set_comprehension` still TAKES the
# `Option[Box[SpannedExpr]]` filter parameter and is correct at stage 1
# because it unpacks with a bare `*sv_fb`. Change that ONE line to
# `(*sv_fb).clone()` and THIS cell goes RED at stage 1 (`0/false/false` for
# `2/true/true`) while all 39 stage-0 cells stay green — measured, and the
# cleanest demonstration in the tree that the hazard is the CLONE, not the
# boxed parameter. Do not "tidy" that unpack.
#
# The wired test `self_host_comprehension_stage1_net` builds a STAGE-1
# binary and runs this cell through it — that is the only instrument that
# sees the class.
#
# The `.len()` assertion is KEPT beside the element read on purpose: for this
# class the LENGTH is the observable (a dropped filter changes the count),
# while the element read is what catches a mint defect.
#
# RED-VERIFIED: at HEAD this cell prints `0/false/false` where `2/true/true`
# is correct — at stage 0 (the §4 silent drop) AND at stage 1.
#
# FIXTURE PLACEMENT: subdirectory (see any NET A cell's header).
# LANE: self-host only.  STAGE: 0 AND 1.  RUNG: 1a (both real lanes agree).

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s0 = mk("ab", "c")
    auto v = {c for c in s0 if c != mk("b", "")}
    print(v.len())
    print(v.contains(mk("a", "")))
    print(v.contains(mk("c", "")))
